From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:32:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): tell agents with the tools to raise and
 close items with them

Agents follow the item-label instruction, which has them pick label
numbers themselves and close an item only by striking it in chat. With
the open items tools available, that would leave the store unused and
the numbers made up.

Agents whose spec keeps the open_items tool group now get a second part
after the item-label instruction: raise items with sys_open_items_raise
before presenting them and write each with the returned label, never
pick a number, adopt a label already written in chat by raising it with
that label, close with sys_open_items_update and a one-line resolution
and then strike the label in chat, list instead of relying on memory,
and still write every item and close in chat. It ends with the fallback:
without the tools, label in chat only. SDK harnesses get it every turn,
right after the item-label instruction; native harnesses get it at
launch, after the stable guidance (build_native_startup_instructions is
wrapped rather than edited, so guidance other changes add to its list
composes with it). The
runner drops the group when the server does not store open items, so
those sessions, and launches without a spec, keep the text-only
instruction. A CLI-launched claude-native or codex-native session
composes its instruction from its local wrapper spec, so there the
fallback sentence covers a server without the feature.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
